Because, by law in most states, the one thing that makes group coverage
so attractive is that, in general, a member of the group can't be turned
down over a pre-existing condition.

Not too much diabetes and heart disease in that crowd.

So the question behind the question is this: how can I ensure that my
family retains adequate health coverage until I find another job that
offers group health coverage, without breaking the bank?
